{:paths ["src"]
 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 ;; Clojure, and nothing else.
 ;;
 ;; That is a statement about the subject rather than minimalism for its own
 ;; sake. This lab argues that configuration must not grow into a second
 ;; programming language, and the closed check in `rules.clj` that enforces it
 ;; is fifteen lines of `clojure.core`. Reaching for a schema library to police
 ;; the shape of configuration would make the argument in prose while
 ;; contradicting it in `deps.edn` -- and it would hide the check behind an
 ;; abstraction, when the whole point is that you can read it.
 ;;
 ;; Everything here is also pure and deterministic. No clock, no `random-uuid`,
 ;; no I/O. That is load bearing rather than tidy: a lab whose claim is *an
 ;; unstamped decision re-runs differently* has to be able to re-run a decision
 ;; and get a byte-identical answer, or it cannot tell you which difference was
 ;; the configuration's fault.
 ;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 :deps  {org.clojure/clojure {:mvn/version "1.12.5"}}
 :aliases
 {:test {:extra-paths ["test"]
         :extra-deps  {lambdaisland/kaocha {:mvn/version "1.91.1392"}}
         :main-opts   ["-m" "kaocha.runner"]}
  :demo {:extra-paths ["dev"]
         :main-opts   ["-m" "lab33.demo"]}}}
